 *   letters are not the trademark, the stylised sphere is. The PlayStation
 *   shapes are drawn as plain strokes in OUR ink, at OUR weight, as nominative
 *   use: they identify which physical button your thumb is on, which is the
 *   whole job of an accessibility device. A pad we do not recognise gets our
 *   own N/E/S/W — the board's own vocabulary, and nobody else's mark.
